  "decision_conditions": [
    "<div>The proposed development, by means of its design, would unduly impact the original design characteristics of the host dwelling. It would disrupt the original building line and would not sympathise with the local context. The proposal would appear visually intrusive and out-keeping with the local distinctiveness and historic character of the&nbsp;Becontree Estate, therefore causing detrimental harm to the non-designated heritage asset. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character:</div><div><br></div><div><ul><li style=\"\">National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024) </li><li style=\"\">Policies&nbsp;D4 and HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) </li><li style=\"\">The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) </li><li style=\"\">Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)</li></ul></div>"
